the question we've been hearing a lot  lately about computer science and being  a software developer is should I go to  school or not is it worth it to get a  bachelor's degree or a master's degree  or PhD in computer science a lot of  people are wondering this do I go to  university to get a job or do I just do  it well the short answer is you just do  it I've been at school for a good four  years straight and I've changed a lot in  this four years it's been very  beneficial to me I think school is worth  it if you're having a little trouble  with motivation or direction if you have  motivation already and if you have  direction already you don't really need  school that badly because you're already  going out and getting the experience you  need school is basically to help you get  experience another thing that tends to  have from a school that doesn't happen  so much in the real world is and school  you end up taking a lot of time and just  like reading and going to lectures and  kind of just kind of sitting there and  not actually a whole lot of doing  usually what tends to happen that gets  you doing is suddenly the teacher  assigned something and gives it a  deadline for what it's due and that gets  you going and motivated to do research  on your own and figure out the problem  and if you do take the time to do  research on your own and figure out  these problems you will learn a lot a  lot but you won't learn much from going  to the lectures and you won't learn much  from reading the assigned stuff it's  from doing the actual projects at least  this is how it was for me what this has  led me to believe is that if you just  already have the motivation and are  already doing projects and it's working  for you you don't need to pay thousands  of dollars a semester to go to school  just to sit in the lectures and read the  assigned stuff main thing that get  actually gets you learn as projects if  you're giving yourself projects that's  great there's also tons of stuff online  tons of tutorials online I think school  is gonna be very useless in like ten  years really soon the internet and just  the plethora of data out there on  anything you want to research  it's pretty amazing people that realize  these things I've said will not continue  out of schools it's just a waste of  money you can be out earning money and  learning your trade at the same time I  think that's very true with computer  science there are some stipulations here  computer science it's not the easiest  thing and when I say computer science  I'm saying that because I'm in  specifically a CS degree and I'm talking  swiftly about the CS degree but most  software developers don't align with  computer science most of them are web  developers they design and style things  and only use basic math when you get  into computer science you learn about  the architecture of computers and chips  and motherboards and how things really  work and how how different chips and  devices considered delays and and  there's a lot of details that go into it  it is literally the science of computers  it's not about software development  software development plays a big part of  it but as a whole computer science is  more about solving the problems of  computing and designing actual computers  and of course the software is on top of  all that so it gets into a lot of math a  lot of theory and a lot of hardware and  most most college degrees that do  computer science require a lot of math  and a lot of additional sciences and  these are pretty useless for software  development almost entirely  [Music]  the classes I have enjoyed are the ones  that gave me programming projects every  time and in my own time in the during  the summer when I had no school I did my  own projects I just decided things I  wanted to do and started to create them  it was really going to school that  introduced me to a lot of the things I  needed to get started I didn't know  where to start so that's why it's been  really really useful for me but at the  same time now they've gone through and a  lot of research I see why it could be  useless to some people as well if you  have any questions let me know I hope  you have a good day and thanks for  watching my video peace out  you  [Music]  you
 

